<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tian An</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 206 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian">Tian</a> An was a grandson of King Jian, the last king of the State of Qi, who fought in the rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> and followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> to Julu. In Xiang Yu's settlement of 206 BCE he was made King of Jibei, north of the Ji River, but within months <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-rong">Tian Rong</a>, excluded from the settlement, attacked and killed him and reunited Qi.</p></div>
